    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87055" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προδῐκ-έω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόδικος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be a
				patron, advocate,</i> or <i>guardian,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ἀλλοτρίου ἀπελευθέρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					100
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.787b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				973a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν τούτου τέκνων</span>
			Mitteis <i><span class="en">
				<u>Chr.</u>
				88 i 15
			</span></i><span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἐνύδρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.975c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>act as advocate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρ . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>GDI</u>
					1432b5
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Hypata</span>).</div>
